{"appendix":false,"contribution_target":{"fingerprint":"sha256:b2727e4bd06f0ac73a4ab81b9cf6e288e236e6485c95a238aa24192f55aa7ee0","grain":"paper-statement","id":"The-PCP-for-PPAD-conjecture-a-quasilinear-reduction-September-25-2026#thm:main","title":"Quasilinear PCP for PPAD"},"credit":{"kind":"producer-declared","license":null,"license_status":"consult-source-notice","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","repository":"https://github.com/openai/math","source":"lean/formalization.yaml","source_registry":"index.json#/sources"},"detail":{"path":"../rows/ae2d779e19e10ff4fed7a6a5.json","pointer":"/row"},"display":"Theorem","generation_id":"sha256:c701139844a2d825c371ded7486924e7dae7de0af77a69dc9c1abaf1129191a1","id":"r:The-PCP-for-PPAD-conjecture-a-quasilinear-reduction-September-25-2026:thm:main","kind":"statement-detail","manuscript_id":"p:The-PCP-for-PPAD-conjecture-a-quasilinear-reduction-September-25-2026","name":"Quasilinear PCP for PPAD","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","printed_number":"1.3","printed_number_provenance":{"atlas_pin":"f047bac96ee80ebef0b4f5a403831b84de6e32c1","binding":{"file":"build/sections/01-introduction.tex","label":"thm:main","line":147,"manuscript":"The-PCP-for-PPAD-conjecture-a-quasilinear-reduction-September-25-2026","statement_sha256":"4be348aee3aa6b633614339b89bb2a367adac4c5108b0fa0eba5c3c94fc1db2d"},"blob_sha256":"sha256:253ae0683558fd095a71d6f47ab0694d8d98b846c1a65d2bbf9b145d484af567","kind":"reading-page-computed","pdf_verified":false,"pin":"f047bac96ee80ebef0b4f5a403831b84de6e32c1","renderer":"scripts/build_papers.py","source":"data/statement_numbers.json","upstream_pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb"},"printed_number_status":"recorded","reading_page":"papers/The-PCP-for-PPAD-conjecture-a-quasilinear-reduction-September-25-2026.html#thm:main","release_id":"openai-math","schema":"statement-map-web/2","section":1,"section_title":"Introduction and the exact search relation","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:c5811bd67d846e6ec9d6e003971462f82b30db7841e5562530e6e61b18c6a3b2","file":"preprints/The-PCP-for-PPAD-conjecture-a-quasilinear-reduction-September-25-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":147,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"4be348aee3aa6b633614339b89bb2a367adac4c5108b0fa0eba5c3c94fc1db2d","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/The-PCP-for-PPAD-conjecture-a-quasilinear-reduction-September-25-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:c5811bd67d846e6ec9d6e003971462f82b30db7841e5562530e6e61b18c6a3b2","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/The-PCP-for-PPAD-conjecture-a-quasilinear-reduction-September-25-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L147"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nThere are fixed rational constants\n\\[\n 0<\\eps<\\tfrac1{10},\\qquad 0<\\delta<1,\n\\]\na fixed positive integer $A$, a fixed nonnegative integer $b$, a fixed\npolynomial $p$ with nonnegative integer coefficients, and deterministic\nalgorithms $R,D$ with the following properties.\n\\begin{enumerate}[label=\\textup{(\\roman*)}]\n\\item Every generalized circuit in Definition~\\ref{def:gcircuit} has an\nacceptable rational assignment of encoding length at most $p(M)$.\n\\item For every End-of-Line instance $I$ of length $N$, the output $R(I)$\nis a generalized circuit whose complete encoding length satisfies\n\\[\n M\\leq A N\\bigl\\lceil\\log_2(N+2)\\bigr\\rceil^b.\n\\]\n\\item The construction $R$ runs in time polynomial in $N$, with one fixed\npolynomial bound.\n\\item For every acceptable assignment $x$ of $R(I)$, the algorithm $D(I,x)$\nreturns a solution of $I$ in time polynomial in $N$ plus the encoding\nlength of $x$, with one fixed polynomial bound.\n\\end{enumerate}\nAll constants, polynomials, and algorithms are chosen once. They use no\nadvice depending on the input length and no randomized construction."}
